# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# Git's default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites these to CRLF, and
# bash then fails on the shebang with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` — an error
# that reads like a broken script rather than a line-ending problem. It bites
# exactly the reader following the WSL2 or Git Bash path in docs/quick-start.md,
# who has no reason to suspect their checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for files consumed inside Linux containers.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
